ssues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.6.stable.official [89cea1439]\nv4.8.dev3.official [51105ccbe]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev3 - macOS Sequoia (15.7.5) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M4 (Apple9) - Apple M4 (10 threads) - 16.00 GiB memory - CoreAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nGlobal constants are always part of enums or bitflags AFAI can see, so they're always `int`s. Therefore there shouldn't be autocompletion for them. But there is (showing constants from the same enum):\n<img width=\"296\" height=\"181\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ae692d2f-0f90-491c-b375-c7e56e239642\" />\n\nI don't see why this is needed for anything (especially since it gives an error: `Cannot get property from enum value.`), so it's clearly a bug. Practically, this is rare to run into, but it can happen by accident when typing quickly, and it feels strange.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nType `var k = KEY_0.` anywhere in a script.\n\nIt shows autocompletion like above.\n\nI discovered this while working on #111010.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_u